From 33783349e8a64480f4c07bd0c8764d68241252cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:09:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/94] cpufreq: qcom-hw: msm8998: request a corner before
 starting the OSM

The OSM is started with whatever the boot chain left in the performance
state register and with no request of our own, so it comes up with no
transition to run: it stays parked on the alternate clock source and
every corner requested afterwards is accepted into the register and
never acted on.  Both clusters then deliver cpu_hw_rate for the whole
frequency ladder.

Request the first performance state before setting the enable bit, which
is what the vendor driver does.  The first entry is the lowest corner and
is sourced from the alternate clock, so it is safe to ask for before the
CPRh loop is armed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index 49522d746..20112af41 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -1615,6 +1615,16 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_hw_osm_setup(struct device *cpu_dev,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Request the lowest performance state before starting the OSM, so
+	 * that it has a corner to converge on the moment it comes up.  Left
+	 * unwritten, the register holds whatever the boot chain put there and
+	 * the OSM has no transition to run: it stays on the alternate source
+	 * it was parked on and every later request is accepted and ignored.
+	 * The first entry is always the safe one, so this needs no CPRh vote.
+	 */
+	writel(0, drv_data->base + qcom_cpufreq.soc_data->reg_perf_state);
+
 	/* We're ready: enable the OSM and give it time to boot (5uS) */
 	writel(1, drv_data->base + qcom_cpufreq.soc_data->reg_enable);
 	udelay(OSM_BOOT_TIME_US);
